<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<CustomField xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS COMMENT SITS INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT DELIBERATELY. A comment placed ABOVE
        <CustomField> breaks `sf` deploy at source conversion with a misleading "unable to find
        matching parent xml file" error.

        DISPOSITION GAP CLOSURE TRANCHE 1, ITEM 1 (agent-output/disposition-gap-closure-t1-design.md
        §3 Item 1). Machine-written audit fact: WHO approved this NDA for release and WHEN.
        Paired with Principal_Approved_Date__c. The approval PROCESS ITSELF (who may set these two
        fields, and how) is Tranche 3 and is NOT designed or built here - this field and its date
        sibling are schema only, with no writer in this tranche.

        =====================================================================================
        🔴 THIS OBJECT ALREADY HAS A REPRESENTATION OF "A PRINCIPAL APPROVED THIS NDA" - RECORD
        THAT NOW SO TRANCHE 3 DOES NOT REDISCOVER IT.
        =====================================================================================
        The Disposition_NDA record type carries Status__c = 'Approved' as a lifecycle position
        (Prepare -> Approved -> Sent -> Signed, Declined terminal, no default - see
        objects/NDA__c/fields/Status__c.field-meta.xml and
        objects/NDA__c/recordTypes/Disposition_NDA.recordType-meta.xml). After this field is added,
        the object holds TWO representations of the same real-world event, deliberately:

            Status__c = 'Approved'          the LIFECYCLE POSITION. Drives the Path. A picklist
                                             VALUE - it cannot carry a timestamp or an audit trail.
            Principal_Approved__c + date    the MACHINE-WRITTEN AUDIT FACT (who/when). A workflow
                                             field update cannot capture "who" - that is precisely
                                             why ApprovalAuditService exists elsewhere in this repo.

        Tranche 3's final approval action should set BOTH — the stage-position picklist AND this
        audit pair — in the same transaction. Do not treat one as redundant with the other.

        =====================================================================================
        FLS (to be applied in the consolidated permission-set pass, not this file).
        =====================================================================================
        Read in DPEG_Disposition_View. READ-ONLY in DPEG_Disposition_Edit too (editable=false) -
        this is an approval-written fact, not an analyst judgement. Precedent:
        BOV_Broker_Change__c's 2026-08-20 code-review reconciliation, which refused an
        allowEdit grant on a similarly approval-written field on the grounds that "granting
        allowEdit would let the very analyst who replaced a broker go back and rewrite who did it
        and when." A Metadata-API-deployed field carries NO FLS for anyone, System Administrator
        included, until that pass lands.

        Risk: LOW. Two new fields, no reader and no writer in T1.
    -->
    <fullName>Principal_Approved__c</fullName>
    <defaultValue>false</defaultValue>
    <description>Machine-written audit fact: TRUE once a principal has approved this NDA for release. Distinct from Status__c = &apos;Approved&apos;, which is the lifecycle position that drives the Path. Tranche 3&apos;s approval action sets both together. See the XML comment in this file.</description>
    <inlineHelpText>Ticked by the approval process once a principal has approved this NDA for release. This is the audit fact, not the Path position - see Status.</inlineHelpText>
    <label>Principal Approved</label>
    <trackHistory>false</trackHistory>
    <trackTrending>false</trackTrending>
    <type>Checkbox</type>
</CustomField>
